          "evidence": "Jobber has not raised new funding since its $61M growth equity round in March 2024 and is reported to be near cash-flow positive. With 1,200-1,359 employees and $167.5M ARR, unit economics appear improving. However, Jobbers per-user pricing model means cost scales with headcount, and there is no evidence of proprietary infrastructure or technology that creates a structural cost advantage.",
